    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0428" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/991</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-20T22:00:00+02:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 20, 1918, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 23, 6.40
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2260. American woman, Russian born, telephoned this afternoon had important
                    information to impart, but afraid to visit Embassy. Sent to see her, were told
                    Embassy be attacked by anarchists and burned to-night, whereupon sent for guard,
                    and ten soldiers here now. Report probably not true but thought precaution
                    wise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
